1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,480
Franchise applications arrive as a spreadsheet, and someone reads and matches every row by hand.

2
00:00:06,883 --> 00:00:12,535
This engine reads the file, checks every applicant, and ranks them within their territory.

3
00:00:12,939 --> 00:00:14,748
Every status has a reason.

4
00:00:14,898 --> 00:00:20,076
Press Why to see each check, where the rule comes from, and how the score adds up.

5
00:00:21,685 --> 00:00:25,411
One rule never bends: no two stores on one pin code.

6
00:00:25,712 --> 00:00:30,333
When two qualified applicants want the same pin, the tool does not pick.

7
00:00:30,483 --> 00:00:32,478
A person makes the final call.

8
00:00:32,848 --> 00:00:36,649
Territories show open slots, free pins and the waitlist.

9
00:00:37,055 --> 00:00:42,763
Settings keeps the rubric editable, with case rules marked apart from our own choices.

10
00:00:43,170 --> 00:00:46,163
The chat answers why questions from the same ledger.

11
00:00:47,566 --> 00:00:53,547
Onboarding starts only after the agreement, GST and legal registrations are ticked.

12
00:00:53,963 --> 00:00:58,767
Built by Namratha Reddy and Vishweshwar, for the MESA Ops Hackathon.
